+
+# 🌐 API Design & REST Architecture Standards
+
+These standards govern public and internal HTTP/REST API endpoints, routing architecture, DTO schemas, authentication contracts, and observability conventions across all backend frameworks.
+
+---
+
+## 1. Resource URI Naming Conventions
+
+- **Nouns, Not Verbs:** URIs represent resources, not actions.
+  - ✅ `GET /api/v1/users`
+  - ❌ `GET /api/v1/getUsers` or `POST /api/v1/deleteUser`
+- **Plural Form:** Always use plural nouns for collection endpoints (`/users`, `/organizations`, `/invoices`).
+- **Kebab-Case:** Lowercase, hyphen-separated multi-word resource names:
+  - ✅ `/api/v1/user-profiles`
+  - ❌ `/api/v1/userProfiles`, `/api/v1/user_profiles`
+- **Nesting Depth Limit (Max 3 Levels):**
+  - ✅ `/api/v1/teams/{team_id}/members` (depth 2)
+  - ❌ `/api/v1/organizations/{org_id}/teams/{team_id}/projects/{proj_id}/tasks`
+  - Flatten deep hierarchies: `/api/v1/projects/{proj_id}/tasks`.
+- **Filtering & Search in Query Parameters:** Never encode filters into path segments.
+  - ✅ `GET /api/v1/products?category=electronics&status=active`
+  - ❌ `GET /api/v1/products/category/electronics/active`
+
+---
+
+## 2. HTTP Methods & Idempotency Matrix
+
+| Method | Purpose | Idempotent | Safe | Request Body |
+|---|---|---|---|---|
+| **`GET`** | Read single resource or collection | ✅ | ✅ | ❌ Forbidden |
+| **`POST`** | Create resource / invoke RPC action | ❌ | ❌ | ✅ Required |
+| **`PUT`** | Complete replacement of a resource | ✅ | ❌ | ✅ Required |
+| **`PATCH`** | Partial update (⚠️ depends on patch format — JSON Merge Patch is idempotent, JSON Patch is not) | ⚠️ | ❌ | ✅ Required |
+| **`DELETE`** | Remove a resource | ✅ | ❌ | ❌ None |
+| **`HEAD`** | Headers only (metadata / existence) | ✅ | ✅ | ❌ Forbidden |
+
+- **No `GET` with side effects.** State mutation over `GET` is forbidden.
+- **No method tunneling.** `X-HTTP-Method-Override` and similar hacks are forbidden.
+
+---
+
+## 3. HTTP Status Codes Standards
+
+### 3.1. Success (2xx)
+- **`200 OK`** — Standard success for `GET`, `PATCH`, `PUT`.
+- **`201 Created`** — Successful `POST` that creates a resource. MUST include a `Location` header.
+- **`202 Accepted`** — Long-running async task initiated; returns task ID / status URL.
+- **`204 No Content`** — Success with no body (typically `DELETE` or action triggers).
+
+### 3.2. Client Errors (4xx)
+- **`400 Bad Request`** — Malformed syntax, unparseable payload.
+- **`401 Unauthorized`** — Missing / expired / invalid authentication credentials.
+- **`403 Forbidden`** — Authenticated but not permitted.
+- **`404 Not Found`** — Target resource does not exist.
+- **`409 Conflict`** — State conflict (unique constraint, concurrent update, idempotency-key reuse with different body).
+- **`422 Unprocessable Entity`** — Valid syntax, failed business validation (Pydantic / schema error).
+- **`429 Too Many Requests`** — Rate limit exceeded. MUST include `Retry-After`.
+
+### 3.3. Server Errors (5xx)
+- **`500 Internal Server Error`** — Unexpected runtime error. Never expose stack traces in production.
+- **`502 Bad Gateway` / `503 Service Unavailable`** — Upstream failure or maintenance.
+
+---
+
+## 4. Request & Response DTO Separation
+
+- **Never Reuse Models.** Declare distinct schemas per operation:
+
+  ```python
+  class UserCreate(BaseModel):
+      email: EmailStr
+      password: str = Field(..., min_length=8)
+      full_name: str
+
+  class UserUpdate(BaseModel):
+      email: EmailStr | None = None
+      full_name: str | None = None
+
+  class UserResponse(BaseModel):
+      id: str
+      email: EmailStr
+      full_name: str
+      created_at: datetime
+      # password is NOT present
+  ```
+
+- **No Server-Generated Fields in Input.** Clients must not supply `id`, `created_at`, `hashed_password`, etc.
+- **Validation at Boundaries.** All DTOs MUST be validated via declarative schemas — see `03-python.md` §2.
+
+---
+
+## 5. Standardized Error Response Envelope
+
+All API errors follow a single JSON shape:
+
+```json
+{
+  "error": {
+    "code": "VALIDATION_ERROR",
+    "message": "The provided input payload is invalid.",
+    "request_id": "req_01h7x89q2m...",
+    "details": [
+      { "field": "email", "issue": "Invalid email address format." }
+    ]
+  }
+}
+```
+
+- **`code`** — Machine-readable uppercase identifier for client routing.
+- **`message`** — Human-readable explanation, safe to surface.
+- **`request_id`** — Correlation ID matched against server logs.
+- **`details`** — Optional array of field-level errors.
+- **Leakage Rule:** The envelope MUST NOT echo internal stack traces, SQL errors, or upstream provider messages verbatim.
+
+---
+
+## 6. Pagination, Filtering, and Sorting
+
+### 6.1. Pagination Envelope
+
+```json
+{
+  "items": [ ... ],
+  "pagination": {
+    "page": 1,
+    "page_size": 20,
+    "total_items": 142,
+    "total_pages": 8,
+    "has_next": true
+  }
+}
+```
+
+- **Offset Pagination** (`page` + `page_size`) — jumpable datasets, low write frequency.
+- **Cursor Pagination** (`cursor` + `limit`) — high-velocity streams (events, feeds).
+- **Hard Cap:** `page_size` MUST have a server-enforced maximum (e.g., 100). Unbounded queries are forbidden.
+
+### 6.2. Sorting
+Standardized URL query params: `sort=created_at:desc` or `sort=-created_at`. Whitelist sortable fields — never pass user input directly into `ORDER BY` (see `02-no-crutches.md` §13).
+
+---
+
+## 7. Versioning & Evolution
+
+- **URL Path Versioning:** Prefix all endpoints with the major version (`/api/v1/...`).
+- **Backward Compatibility Invariant:** Never remove fields or change field types within a major version. New major versions (`/api/v2/`) only for breaking structural changes.
+- **Deprecation Headers:**
+  - `Deprecation: @1735689600` (Unix timestamp)
+  - `Sunset: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 00:00:00 GMT`
+  - `Link: <https://api.example.com/docs/v2-migration>; rel="sunset"`
+
+---
+
+## 8. Asynchronous Route Handler Safety
+
+- **Non-Blocking I/O:** `async def` handlers MUST NOT execute synchronous blocking operations (`requests.get()`, `time.sleep()`, sync DB drivers). Use `httpx.AsyncClient` and async ORM drivers.
+- **Dependency Injection:** DB sessions, external clients, and auth contexts are managed via DI (`Depends(get_db)`) with strict cleanup on error paths (`try/finally`, `async with`).
+- **No Blocking CPU Work:** Heavy computation belongs in a worker pool, not the event loop.
+
+---
+
+## 9. Authentication & Authorization
+
+- **Token Transport:** Bearer tokens ONLY via `Authorization: Bearer <token>` over HTTPS. Tokens in query strings, URL fragments, or non-`HttpOnly` cookies are forbidden.
+- **401 vs 403:** Never conflate — `401` = missing/invalid credentials; `403` = authenticated but unauthorized.
+- **Boundary Enforcement:** Authorization is enforced at route boundaries (middleware / DI dependency), never delegated to client or buried in business logic.
+- **No Custom Crypto:** Never implement custom encryption, token signing, or password hashing. Use vetted libraries (`PyJWT`, `python-jose`, `passlib`, `bcrypt`).
+- **Cross-Reference:** Secret handling follows `02-no-crutches.md` §12.
+
+---
+
+## 10. Idempotency for Non-Idempotent Operations
+
+- **`Idempotency-Key` Header:** Clients MAY send `Idempotency-Key: <uuid>` on `POST`. The server MUST persist the key + response for a bounded TTL (e.g., 24h) and replay the cached response on duplicate keys.
+- **Required Scope:** Payments, order creation, and any operation with external side effects.
+- **Conflict Response:** Reusing a key with a *different* request body MUST return `409 Conflict`.
+
+---
+
+## 11. Caching & Conditional Requests
+
+- **`ETag` on GET:** Single-resource `GET` responses SHOULD carry a strong `ETag`.
+- **Conditional GET:** Honor `If-None-Match`; return `304 Not Modified` on match.
+- **Sensitive Responses:** Authenticated user data MUST set `Cache-Control: private, no-store`.
+- **Public Static:** `Cache-Control: public, max-age=..., immutable` for content-hashed assets.
+
+---
+
+## 12. Rate Limiting & Throttling
+
+- **Standard Headers:** Return `X-RateLimit-Limit`, `X-RateLimit-Remaining`, `X-RateLimit-Reset` on every response.
+- **`429` Response:** MUST include `Retry-After` (seconds or HTTP date).
+- **Scoping:** Enforce per authenticated principal for authenticated routes; per-IP only for anonymous traffic.
+
+---
+
+## 13. CORS Policy
+
+- **No Wildcard + Credentials:** `Access-Control-Allow-Origin: *` MUST NOT be combined with `Access-Control-Allow-Credentials: true`.
+- **Explicit Allow-List:** Allowed origins live in configuration (env / config file), never hardcoded inline.
+- **Preflight:** `OPTIONS` handlers return proper `Access-Control-Allow-Methods` / `-Headers`; cache via `Access-Control-Max-Age`.
+
+---
+
+## 14. Request Tracing & Observability
+
+- **Request ID Propagation:** Every inbound request receives a `request_id` (from `X-Request-ID` or generated). Propagated downstream; echoed in error envelope (§5).
+- **Structured Logging:** Emit structured fields (see `03-python.md` §3): `request_id`, `route`, `method`, `status`, `latency_ms`, `user_id`.
+- **Never Log:** Authorization headers, cookies, PII, passwords, full card numbers.
+- **Latency Budgets:** Track p50/p95/p99 per route; regressions are treated as bugs.
+
+---
+
+## 15. API Documentation (OpenAPI)
+
+- **Schema-First:** OpenAPI 3.x is generated from the same DTO models used at runtime (Pydantic → OpenAPI, Zod → OpenAPI). Handwritten specs that drift are forbidden.
+- **Coverage:** Every endpoint declares a summary, request DTO, success response, and all applicable error responses.
+- **Deprecation:** Deprecated routes flagged in spec (`deprecated: true`) and cross-referenced with headers (§7).
+
+---
+
+## 16. Data Access Patterns (N+1 Prevention)
+
+- **No Per-Item Queries in Loops:** Fetching related records inside a loop is forbidden. Use eager loading (`joinedload`, `selectinload`), batch fetching, or `IN (...)`.
+- **Bounded Result Sets:** All collection endpoints MUST be paginated (§6). No unbounded `SELECT *`.
+- **Streaming:** Large exports (CSV, binary) stream via chunked responses — never buffer fully in memory.
+- **Cross-Reference:** Module decomposition rules — `01-architecture.md` §1.
